\section{EXPERIMENTS}
\label{sec:experiments}
\subsection{Data and Implementation}
The UterUS dataset~\cite{bones2024automatic} comprises 3D US volumes with binary uterine-region masks, excluding cases with fibroids, adenomyosis, and other acquired abnormalities. 
The Uterine Myoma MRI Dataset (UMD)~\cite{pan2024umd} provides labels for the \textit{uterine wall}, \textit{uterine cavity}, \textit{myoma}, and \textit{Nabothian cyst} (when present) on T2-weighted MRI of patients with surgically and pathologically confirmed fibroids.
Training/validation/held-out test sets contain 100/10/28 cases for UterUS and 191/21/54 for UMD. Following MultiTalent~\cite{ulrich2023multitalent}, we adopt its nnU-Net-based preprocessing~\cite{isensee2021nnunet} (1-mm isotropic resampling and z-score normalization) and data augmentation. Training uses $192^3$ patches, batch size 1, and 1,000 epochs of 250 iterations with Nesterov SGD (momentum 0.99, weight decay $3\!\times\!10^{-5}$; polynomial decay from $10^{-3}$). All methods share splits, preprocessing, and postprocessing. Dice and average symmetric surface distance (ASSD) are reported as mean$\pm$SD over cases per foreground class, then macro-averaged; ASSD is omitted for empty surfaces.
