\subsection{Qualitative Visual Grounding}
To illustrate the mechanism behind these quantitative gains, Figure \ref{fig:qualitative} presents a representative B-mode ultrasound case from the colon-wall-stratification task with ground-truth label "lost." Queried directly, GPT-5.4 hedges between competing visual interpretations and concludes an incorrect diagnosis. Under the ARISE workflow, the same underlying model grounds its answer in concrete, vocabulary-anchored observations ("the bowel wall appears diffusely hypoechoic and homogeneous, with no separable alternating layers or consistent banding along the segment") and correctly predicts "lost." This case is typical of the pattern underlying the quantitative improvements described earlier: ARISE's evidence-summarization (S2) and symbolic-verification (S4) stages guide the model away from ambiguous, hedged visual claims and toward grounded and verifiable ones, which is where the framework's accuracy gains originate.
