\suppnote{Exploratory phenotype-stratified analysis of TCH-SHD predictions}{si-note:shd-phenotypes}
The primary TCH-SHD endpoint was binary study-level classification of the prespecified \texttt{SHD\_any} composite, rather than diagnosis-specific prediction. To examine how this binary prediction behaved across component phenotypes, we calculated, for each non-mutually-exclusive label, the proportion of label-positive studies classified as \texttt{SHD\_any}. This post hoc analysis describes phenotype-stratified recall of the composite classifier; it does not estimate phenotype-specific false-positive rates, discrimination, or diagnostic performance. Label support ranged from $n=1$ to $n=202$ studies, so estimates for rare phenotypes should be interpreted as exploratory.
